   "what_the_market_was_braced_for": "The market expected SentinelOne to report Q2 FY2027 non-GAAP EPS of ~$0.07 on revenue of ~$290.25M (top end of the company's own $289-291M guidance), with the key focus on forward guidance: Q3 non-GAAP EPS of ~$0.11 on revenue of ~$309.4M and FY2027 non-GAAP EPS of ~$0.35 on revenue of ~$1.205B. The stock had run up ~8.4% over the five sessions before the print amid a broader cybersecurity rally, implying elevated expectations. The market was braced for continued ARR acceleration and operating leverage; headlines indicate the print beat Q2 estimates but guidance disappointed (Q3 EPS guided to $0.08-$0.09 vs $0.11 est; FY EPS cut to $0.30-$0.32 vs $0.35 est), sending shares lower.",
